     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Blocking fileServer:lateralMovement, rdpLogin:authenticate and hypervisor:privilegeEscalation makes the target unreachable. (1) Blocking fileServer cuts codeRepo, and with it secretsManager and therefore vaultRead. (2) Blocking rdpLogin cuts domainAdmin, which removes mailArchive and one route to dbReplica, and also cuts secretsManager. (3) Blocking hypervisor cuts the last route to dbReplica. Two blocks are not enough because there are three separate attack paths with no shared blockable step. Path A: tokenCache -> fileServer -> codeRepo. Path B: apiToken + rdpLogin -> domainAdmin -> mailArchive. Path C: configSecret -> monitoringHost, plus vpnSession -> printServer, both feeding hypervisor -> dbReplica. No single step lies on two of these paths, and each needs its own block. So the minimum is 3.\"}"
    }
   ],
